info  {"category":"agent-session","raw":{"timestamp":"2026-08-07T13:08:43.070Z","type":"response_ite
      m","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","call_id":"call_oM27nvEpP6Ge3pR15wxTsvjj","outp
      ut":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0
      seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"# MicroSandbox Workspaces (`msw`) 3.1.0\n\nA
      ready-to-run development setup for an Apple Silicon Mac with three isolated, persistent Linux
      microVM workspaces:\n\n| Workspace | Purpose | Normal live limit | Resize ceiling | Browser
      name |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---|\n| `dev` | Main/work development | 8 CPU, 32 GB RAM | 48 GB
      RAM | `dev.msw.test` |\n| `playgrounds` | Experiments | 4 CPU, 32 GB RAM | 48 GB RAM |
      `playgrounds.msw.test` |\n| `personal` | Personal projects | 6 CPU, 16 GB RAM | 32 GB RAM |
      `personal.msw.test` |\n\nEach workspace has its own Ubuntu system, repositories, Docker
      daemon, images, volumes, credentials, processes, and public-internet connection. Code and
      Docker data live on independent persistent ext4 volumes. Zed and Ghostty remain native macOS
      applications and connect over SSH.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\nunzip
      microsandbox-workspaces-v3.1.0.zip\ncd microsandbox-workspaces\n./setup.sh\nexec zsh
      -l\n```\n\n`setup.sh` installs the host tools, builds the common development image, creates
      all three workspaces, publishes the configured localhost ports, configures SSH/Zed
      integration, and finishes with a live deep check.\n\nThen set your commit
      identity:\n\n```bash\nmsw identity \"Your Name\" you@example.com\n```\n\nConfigure GitHub
      separately for each workspace:\n\n```bash\nmsw github setup dev OWNER/VERIFICATION-REPO\nmsw
      github setup playgrounds OWNER/VERIFICATION-REPO\nmsw github setup personal
      OWNER/VERIFICATION-REPO\n```\n\nEach command asks for two fine-grained GitHub tokens and
      verifies the complete permission boundary automatically: read/clone from the VM, rejected
      guest push, successful host-only push, and cleanup. See
      [`docs/GITHUB-SETUP.md`](docs/GITHUB-SETUP.md).\n\n## Daily use\n\n```bash\n# Enter /workspace
      in Ghostty\nmsw dev\nmsw playgrounds\nmsw personal\n\n# Enter a nested repository\nmsw dev
      clients/acme/backend\n\n# Clone into a nested folder\nmsw clone dev OWNER/REPO
      clients/acme/backend\n\n# Open in Zed\nmsw zed dev clients/acme/backend\n\n# Open a running
      website in your Mac browser\nmsw open dev 3000\nmsw open playgrounds 5173\n\n# Explicitly push
      the current committed branch from the Mac\nmsw push dev clients/acme/backend\n\n# Back up
      every VM and persistent volume\nmsw backup\n```\n\nA service must listen on `0.0.0.0` inside
      the VM or container. The common development ports are already published to each workspace's
      dedicated loopback IP, so all three can use port 3000 simultaneously.\n\n## Documentation\n\n-
      [Complete setup guide](docs/SETUP-GUIDE.md)\n- [GitHub permissions and push
      guide](docs/GITHUB-SETUP.md)\n- [Command cheatsheet](docs/MSW-CHEATSHEET.md)\n- [Test
      report](docs/TEST-REPORT.md)\n\nInstalled documentation is also available from any
      terminal:\n\n```bash\nmsw docs setup\nmsw docs github\nmsw docs cheatsheet\nmsw docs
      tests\n```\n\n## Trust boundary\n\nEvery process and agent inside one workspace can access
      everything in that workspace. The three workspaces are separate from one another and no Mac
      folder, Mac Docker socket, or Mac SSH agent is mounted into them. The guest GitHub credential
      is read-only and host-held; the write credential remains in macOS Keychain and is used only by
      the explicit `msw push` path.\n\nFull public internet access means an untrusted agent can
      still transmit files it can read to an unrelated internet service. This setup prevents direct
      access to your Mac and prevents GitHub pushes with the guest credential; it is not a
      data-loss-prevention system.\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -Eeuo
      pipefail\n\nCONFIG_FILE=\"${MSW_CONFIG_FILE:-$HOME/.config/msw/config.sh}\"\nif [[ ! -f
      \"$CONFIG_FILE\" ]]; then\n printf 'msw: missing %s\\nRun the MicroSandbox Workspaces setup
      installer.\\n' \"$CONFIG_FILE\" >&2\n exit 1\nfi\n# shellcheck source=/dev/null\nsource
      \"$CONFIG_FILE\"\n\nreadonly WORKSPACES=(dev playgrounds personal)\nreadonly
      READ_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE=\"msw.github.read\"\nreadonly
      WRITE_KEYCHAIN_SERVICE=\"msw.github.write\"\nreadonly
      GITHUB_META_DIR=\"$HOME/.config/msw/github\"\nSETUP_TRANSACTION_ACTIVE=0\nSETUP_TRANSACTION_BO
      X=\"\"\nGITHUB_LOCK_HELD=0\n\nMSB_BIN=\"${MSW_MSB_BIN:-$(command -v msb 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nSSH_BIN=\"${MSW_SSH_BIN:-$(command -v ssh 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nCURL_BIN=\"${MSW_CURL_BIN:-$(command -v curl 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nGIT_BIN=\"${MSW_GIT_BIN:-$(command -v git 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nJQ_BIN=\"${MSW_JQ_BIN:-$(command -v jq 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nOPEN_BIN=\"${MSW_OPEN_BIN:-/usr/bin/open}\"\nSECURITY_BIN=\"${MSW_SECURITY_BIN:-/usr
      /bin/security}\"\nASKPASS_BIN=\"${MSW_ASKPASS_BIN:-$HOME/.local/libexec/msw-git-askpass}\"\nGT
      AR_BIN=\"${MSW_GTAR_BIN:-$(command -v gtar 2>/dev/null || command -v tar 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nZSTD_BIN=\"${MSW_ZSTD_BIN:-$(command -v zstd 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nSHASUM_BIN=\"${MSW_SHASUM_BIN:-$(command -v shasum 2>/dev/null ||
      true)}\"\nLOCKF_BIN=\"${MSW_LOCKF_BIN:-$(command -v lockf 2>/dev/null || true)}\"\n\nfatal() {
      printf 'msw: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2; exit 1; }\nnote() { printf '\\033[1;36m==> %s\\033[0m\\n'
      \"$*\"; }\nwarn() { printf '\\033[1;33mwarning: %s\\033[0m\\n' \"$*\" >&2; }\nok() { printf
      '\\033[1;32m✓\\033[0m %s\\n' \"$*\"; }\n\nrequire_command_path() {\n local label=\"$1\"
      value=\"$2\"\n [[ -n \"$value\" && -x \"$value\" ]] || fatal \"'$label' is
      required\"\n}\n\nis_workspace() {\n case \"${1:-}\" in dev|playgrounds|personal) return 0 ;;
      *) return 1 ;; esac\n}\n\nvalidate_workspace() {\n is_workspace \"${1:-}\" || fatal
      \"workspace must be dev, playgrounds, or personal\"\n}\n\nfor_targets() {\n local
      target=\"${1:-all}\" box\n if [[ \"$target\" == all ]]; then\n for box in
      \"${WORKSPACES[@]}\"; do printf '%s\\n' \"$box\"; done\n else\n validate_workspace
      \"$target\"\n printf '%s\\n' \"$target\"\n fi\n}\n\nworkspace_ip() {\n case \"$1\" in\n dev)
      printf '%s\\n' \"$MSW_DEV_IP\" ;;\n playgrounds) printf '%s\\n' \"$MSW_PLAYGROUNDS_IP\" ;;\n
      personal) printf '%s\\n' \"$MSW_PERSONAL_IP\" ;;\n esac\n}\n\nworkspace_host() {\n case \"$1\"
      in\n dev) printf '%s\\n' \"$MSW_DEV_HOST\" ;;\n playgrounds) printf '%s\\n'
      \"$MSW_PLAYGROUNDS_HOST\" ;;\n personal) printf '%s\\n' \"$MSW_PERSONAL_HOST\" ;;\n
      esac\n}\n\nworkspace_ssh_host() { printf '%s.msb\\n' \"$1\"; }\nworkspace_volume() { printf
      'msw-%s-%s\\n' \"$1\" \"$2\"; }\n\nsafe_key_component() { printf '%s' \"$1\" | tr -c
      'A-Za-z0-9_.-' '_'; }\n\nkeychain_test_file() {\n local service account\n
      service=\"$(safe_key_component \"$1\")\"\n account=\"$(safe_key_component \"$2\")\"\n printf
      '%s/%s__%s\\n' \"$MSW_TEST_KEYCHAIN_DIR\" \"$service\" \"$account\"\n}\n\nkeychain_get() {\n
      local service=\"$1\" account=\"$2\"\n if [[ -n \"${MSW_TEST_KEYCHAIN_DIR:-}\" ]]; then\n local
      file\n file=\"$(keychain_test_file \"$service\" \"$account\")\"\n [[ -f \"$file\" ]] || return
      1\n cat \"$file\"\n else\n \"$SECURITY_BIN\" find-generic-password -w -s \"$service\" -a
      \"$account\" 2>/dev/null\n fi\n}\n\nkeychain_has() { keychain_get \"$1\" \"$2\" >/dev/null
      2>&1; }\n\nkeychain_set() {\n local service=\"$1\" account=\"$2\" value=\"$3\"\n if [[ -n
      \"${MSW_TEST_KEYCHAIN_DIR:-}\" ]]; then\n local file\n mkdir -p \"$MSW_TEST_KEYCHAIN_DIR\"\n
      chmod 700 \"$MSW_TEST_KEYCHAIN_DIR\"\n file=\"$(keychain_test_file \"$service\"
      \"$account\")\"\n umask 077\n printf '%s' \"$value\" >\"$file\"\n else\n \"$SECURITY_BIN\"
      add-generic-password -U -s \"$service\" -a \"$account\" -w \"$value\" >/dev/null\n
      fi\n}\n\nkeychain_item_not_found() {\n local status=\"$1\" error=\"$2\"\n [[ \"$status\" == 44
      ]] && return 0\n case \"$error\" in\n *\"The specified item could not be found in the
      keychain.\"*) return 0 ;;\n *) return 1 ;;\n esac\n}\n\nkeychain_delete() {\n local
      service=\"$1\" account=\"$2\" error=\"\" status\n if [[ -n \"${MSW_TEST_KEYCHAIN_DIR:-}\" ]];
      then\n rm -f \"$(keychain_test_file \"$service\" \"$account\")\"\n else\n if
      error=\"$(\"$SECURITY_BIN\" delete-generic-password -s \"$service\" -a \"$account\" 2>&1)\";
      then\n status=0\n else\n status=$?\n fi\n if (( status != 0 )) && ! keychain_item_not_found
      \"$status\" \"$error\"; then\n printf 'msw: could not delete Keychain item %s/%s: %s\\n'
      \"$service\" \"$account\" \"${error:-security exited $status}\" >&2\n return 1\n fi\n if
      error=\"$(\"$SECURITY_BIN\" find-generic-password -w -s \"$service\" -a \"$account\" 2>&1)\";
      then\n printf 'msw: Keychain item still exists %s/%s\\n' \"$service\" \"$account\" >&2\n
      return 1\n else\n status=$?\n fi\n if ! keychain_item_not_found \"$status\" \"$error\"; then\n
      printf 'msw: could not verify Keychain item removal %s/%s: %s\\n' \"$service\" \"$account\"
      \"${error:-security exited $status}\" >&2\n return 1\n fi\n fi\n return
      0\n}\n\nmetadata_file() { printf '%s/%s.conf\\n' \"$GITHUB_META_DIR\" \"$1\";
      }\n\nmetadata_access() {\n local file\n file=\"$(metadata_file \"$1\")\"\n [[ -f \"$file\" ]]
      || return 1\n sed -n 's/^access=//p' \"$file\" | head -n 1\n}\n\nmetadata_repo() {\n local
      file\n file=\"$(metadata_file \"$1\")\"\n [[ -f \"$file\" ]] || return 1\n sed -n
      's/^verification_repo=//p' \"$file\" | head -n 1\n}\n\nwrite_metadata() {\n local box=\"$1\"
      repo=\"$2\" access=\"${3:-host-write}\"\n mkdir -p \"$GITHUB_META_DIR\"\n chmod 700
      \"$GITHUB_META_DIR\"\n umask 077\n printf
      'verification_repo=%s\\naccess=%s\\nconfigured_at=%s\\n' \"$repo\" \"$access\" \"$(date -u
      +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\" >\"$(metadata_file \"$box\")\"\n}\n\nsandbox_exists() { \"$MSB_BIN\"
      inspect \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1; }\nsandbox_inspect_state() {\n local box=\"$1\" output\n if
      output=\"$(\"$MSB_BIN\" inspect \"$box\" 2>&1)\"; then return 0; fi\n [[ \"$output\" ==
      *\"sandbox not found\"* ]] && return 1\n return 2\n}\nsnapshot_exists() { \"$MSB_BIN\"
      snapshot inspect \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1; }\nvolume_exists() { \"$MSB_BIN\" volume inspect
      \"$1\" >/dev/null 2>&1; }\nquarantine_file() { printf '%s/%s.quarantine\\n'
      \"$GITHUB_META_DIR\" \"$1\"; }\ngithub_lock_file() { printf '%s/%s.lock\\n'
      \"$GITHUB_META_DIR\" \"$1\"; }\ngithub_lock_reclaim_legacy() {\n local lock=\"$1\" owner=\"\"
      moved_owner=\"\" stale=\"${lock}.legacy.$$.$RANDOM\"\n if [[ -f \"$lock/pid\" ]]; then\n
      owner=\"$(cat \"$lock/pid\" 2>/dev/null || true)\"\n if [[ \"$owner\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] && kill
      -0 \"$owner\" 2>/dev/null; then return 1; fi\n fi\n [[ ! -e \"$stale\" ]] || return 1\n if !
      mv \"$lock\" \"$stale\" 2>/dev/null; then return 1; fi\n moved_owner=\"$(cat \"$stale/pid\"
      2>/dev/null || true)\"\n if [[ \"$moved_owner\" =~ ^[0-9]+$ ]] && kill -0 \"$moved_owner\"
      2>/dev/null; then\n if [[ ! -e \"$lock\" ]]; then mv \"$stale\" \"$lock\" 2>/dev/null || true;
      fi\n return 1\n fi\n # The rename owns this directory; remove its stale pid before removing
      it.\n if ! rm -f \"$stale/pid\" 2>/dev/null || ! rmdir \"$stale\" 2>/dev/null; then return 1;
      fi\n}\ngithub_lock_release() {\n if (( GITHUB_LOCK_HELD )); then\n exec 9>&-\n
      GITHUB_LOCK_HELD=0\n fi\n trap - EXIT\n}\n\ngithub_lock_exit() {\n local status=\"${1:-1}\"\n
      trap - EXIT\n github_lock_release\n exit \"$status\"\n}\n\ngithub_lock_acquire() {\n local
      box=\"$1\" lock\n require_command_path lockf \"$LOCKF_BIN\"\n mkdir -p \"$GITHUB_META_DIR\" ||
      return 1\n chmod 700 \"$GITHUB_META_DIR\" || return 1\n lock=\"$(github_lock_file
      \"$box\")\"\n if [[ -d \"$lock\" ]]; then\n github_lock_reclaim_legacy \"$lock\" || fatal
      \"GitHub operation already in progress for workspace '$box'\"\n fi\n if ! exec 9>>\"$lock\";
      then return 1; fi\n if ! \"$LOCKF_BIN\" -s -t 0 9; then\n exec 9>&-\n fatal \"GitHub operation
      already in progress for workspace '$box'\"\n fi\n if ! printf '%s\\n' \"$$\" >\"$lock\";
      then\n exec 9>&-\n return 1\n fi\n GITHUB_LOCK_HELD=1\n trap 'github_lock_exit $?'
      EXIT\n}\n\nassert_not_quarantined() {\n local box=\"$1\" file\n [[
      \"${MSW_ALLOW_QUARANTINED:-0}\" == 1 ]] && return 0\n file=\"$(quarantine_file \"$box\")\"\n
      [[ ! -e \"$file\" && ! -L \"$file\" ]] || fatal \"workspace '$box' is quarantined; repair it
      with: msw github setup $box OWNER/REPO\"\n}\n\nsandbox_running() {\n local box=\"$1\" status\n
      status=\"$(\"$MSB_BIN\" status \"$box\" --format json 2>/dev/null)\" || return 2\n
      status=\"$(printf '%s' \"$status\" | tr -d '[:space:]')\"\n case \"$status\" in\n
      *'\"status\":\"Running\"'*) return 0 ;;\n *'\"status\":\"Stopped\"'*) return 1 ;;\n *) return
      2 ;;\n esac\n}\n\nquarantine_workspace() {\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# MicroSandbox Workspaces
      configuration.\n# The installer copies this file to ~/.config/msw/config.sh and preserves
      local edits.\n\nMSW_VERSION=\"3.1.0\"\n\n# Shared base image and immutable development
      snapshot.\nMSW_BASE_IMAGE=\"ghcr.io/superradcompany/ubuntu-systemd:24.04\"\nMSW_BASE_BUILDER=\
      "msw-base-builder\"\nMSW_BASE_SNAPSHOT=\"msw-base-v1\"\nMSW_ROOT_DISK=\"48G\"\n\n# Friendly
      browser names. Each VM has a distinct loopback IP, so identical ports can\n# be used
      concurrently by all workspaces while remaining local to this
      Mac.\nMSW_DEV_IP=\"127.0.0.10\"\nMSW_DEV_HOST=\"dev.msw.test\"\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_IP=\"127.0.0.1
      1\"\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_HOST=\"playgrounds.msw.test\"\nMSW_PERSONAL_IP=\"127.0.0.12\"\nMSW_PERSON
      AL_HOST=\"personal.msw.test\"\n\n# Workspace CPU defaults plus each workspace's live memory
      limit and resize
      ceiling.\nMSW_DEV_CPUS=\"8\"\nMSW_DEV_MAX_CPUS=\"12\"\nMSW_DEV_MEMORY=\"32G\"\nMSW_DEV_MAX_MEM
      ORY=\"48G\"\n\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_CPUS=\"4\"\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_MAX_CPUS=\"12\"\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_ME
      MORY=\"32G\"\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_MAX_MEMORY=\"48G\"\n\nMSW_PERSONAL_CPUS=\"6\"\nMSW_PERSONAL_MAX_
      CPUS=\"12\"\nMSW_PERSONAL_MEMORY=\"16G\"\nMSW_PERSONAL_MAX_MEMORY=\"32G\"\n\n# Independent
      persistent ext4 volumes. Adjust before first installation if
      needed.\nMSW_DEV_WORKSPACE_SIZE=\"120G\"\nMSW_DEV_RUNTIME_SIZE=\"100G\"\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_WORKS
      PACE_SIZE=\"60G\"\nMSW_PLAYGROUNDS_RUNTIME_SIZE=\"60G\"\nMSW_PERSONAL_WORKSPACE_SIZE=\"100G\"\
      nMSW_PERSONAL_RUNTIME_SIZE=\"80G\"\n\n# Published on every workspace's own loopback IP.\n#
      24678 and 24679 are reserved for automated end-to-end health
      tests.\nMSW_PUBLISHED_PORTS=\"1234,1337,24678-24679,3000-3010,3100,3333,3306-3308,4000-4005,41
      73,4200,4321,5001-5005,5173-5180,5432-5435,5555,6006,6379-6382,7001-7005,8000-8010,8080-8090,8
      787,8888,9000-9005,9229-9230,27017-27019\"\n\n# The guest sees a placeholder named GH_TOKEN.
      The real read token stays on the host\n# and is substituted only when traffic reaches one of
      these GitHub
      endpoints.\nMSW_GITHUB_SECRET_HOSTS=\"github.com,api.github.com\"\n\nMSW_BACKUP_DIR=\"$HOME/Ba
      ckups/microsandbox\"\nMSW_DOCS_DIR=\"$HOME/.local/share/msw/docs\"\n"}],"internal_chat_message
